      "band_name": "Mao e la Rivoluzione",
      "bio_additions": "Mao e la Rivoluzione was an Italian alternative rock band from Turin, formed in 1993. The band consisted of Mauro \"Mao\" Gurlino (vocals, guitar), Matteo Salvadori (guitar), Gianluca \"Mago\" Medina (bass), and Paolo \"Gep\" Cucco (drums). They released two albums on Virgin Records (Sale in 1996 and Casa in 1997) and participated in the Sanremo Giovani festival with \"Romantico.\" The band opened for Oasis in 1997. After disbanding in 1998, Mauro Gurlino continued as a solo artist under the name Mao, releasing multiple albums and hosting the long-running live music event \"Il Salotto di Mao\" at LAB Torino since 1997.",
